{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. For node reads, the SDK builds a `Snapshot` from the contents `Domain::node_content` returns. Its fingerprint is those contents' `NodeContents::fingerprint`. It does this without another read.\n2. `Snapshot<T>` has public `content` and `fingerprint` fields, and `Snapshot::new(content, fingerprint)` pairs them.\n3. `Snapshot` is `#[non_exhaustive]` and implements `Clone` (where `T: Clone`) and `Debug` (where `T: Debug`).\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Obligation 1, content and fingerprint.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` calls `read_snapshot`. It asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint` and `snapshot.fingerprint.value == \"before\"`.\n  - The same test changes the graph afterwards and shows the content and fingerprint stay at the earlier version, so they come from the one read.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` covers two input classes: empty and large multi-byte Unicode content. It asserts `snapshot.fingerprint == fp(original)` and that `snapshot.content.format()` equals the original.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts `read_snapshot(&1).unwrap().fingerprint == fp(\"before\")`.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks that `node_content(..).fingerprint()` matches the retained contents' fingerprint, with a pinned scheme and digest.\n- **Obligation 1, no additional read.**\n  - `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` asserts the graph's `reads` list is `[1]` after the snapshot.\n  - `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` asserts `reads == [1, 1]` after one `read_snapshot` and one `read`, which is one read per call.\n  - `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` asserts the read counts `[1, 1, 1, 2]`.\n- **Obligation 1, agent tool path.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` checks that the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprint is built from the content read, including a case where delivery fails. `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks the content/fingerprint pairs recorded for each insertion.\n- **Obligation 2.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` calls `Snapshot::new` and asserts both public fields.\n- **Obligation 3.** `Clone` and `Debug` come from `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` on `struct[Snapshot]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs`. A derive has no conditional or transformation of its own, so it needs no dedicated test. `#[non_exhaustive]` is a compile-time attribute with no runtime behavior. Testing it would need a compile-fail harness, and the requirement states no behavior beyond the declaration.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept. A fingerprint recomputed from a second read, or one that did not match the contents, would fail the equality, read-count and changed-graph assertions listed above. No {fixme} acknowledgments are involved.",
